    Backend: run the background job dequeue at READ COMMITTED
    
    SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED is what gives the job queue its
    mutual exclusion, at any isolation level; the REPEATABLE READ wrapper
    around it added nothing but failure modes. Under REPEATABLE READ the
    dequeue cannot follow the update chain of a row another worker has just
    completed and committed, so it aborts the whole transaction with a
    serialization error rather than stepping over that row. The worker then
    returned no-job and slept, meaning contention made workers idle.
    
    Drops worker_repeatable_read_session_scope (identical to session_scope
    once the isolation override is gone, and unused elsewhere), along with
    the OperationalError catch, which no longer has serialization failures
    to catch and was otherwise swallowing connection errors and reporting
    them as an empty queue.
    
    Removes couchers_background_jobs_serialization_errors_total.
    
