    Take the gallery photo lookup as a parameter, not module state
    
    The single-pass metrics query needs the avatar check as a join rather than a
    correlated EXISTS, which inside an aggregate FILTER stays a subplan and runs
    once per row. That was done with a subquery sitting at module scope in
    completed_profile.py, which is neither where it's needed nor something that
    should exist at import time.
    
    has_completed_profile_expression now takes the subquery as an optional
    parameter and falls back to the EXISTS without one, so every existing caller is
    unchanged. The subquery is a local in the function that builds the users
    gauges, closed over by both the condition and the join.
    
