Author: Aapeli <git@aapelivuorinen.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 1 23:16:01 2026 -0400

    Compute user metrics in a single pass over the users table
    
    The sixteen or so couchers_users_* gauges were each their own SELECT count(*)
    FROM users, adding up to roughly sixteen full sequential scans of the table on
    every scrape and dominating sequential tuple reads in the database. They're now
    counted with count(*) FILTER in one statement, including the by-recency buckets.
    
    Also adds a stored generated users.about_me_length column so profile
    completeness checks never have to detoast about_me, which was the dominant cost
    of both the lite_users refresh and the profile metrics.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

