    Backend: exclude hidden references from the reference count
    
    The reference count on a user's profile (User.num_references) counted all
    references received, but ListReferences hides host/surf references until the
    recipient writes their reciprocal reference or the 2-week writing window
    closes. The count therefore included references the list hides, so a profile
    could show a count of 1 with an empty references list — and the count leaked
    the existence of a still-hidden reference.
    
    Extract the list's visibility rule into a shared reference_publicly_visible()
    helper and apply it in both ListReferences and get_num_references so the two
    can't drift. The list refactor is behaviour-equivalent (correlated EXISTS
    instead of outer joins, which also avoids a latent duplicate-row edge case).
    
    Closes #4946, closes #2374
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

