    mobile: upload pre-generated proto stubs to EAS via root .easignore
    
    The shared-proto-gen refactor expected EAS native builds to consume the proto
    stubs from the GitLab `protos` artifact, "uploaded as-is since .easignore
    doesn't exclude proto/". But eas-cli reads .easignore ONLY from the git
    repository root (path.join(rootPath, EASIGNORE_FILENAME)) and archives from
    there; the app/mobile/.easignore was below that root and never applied. With no
    root .easignore, EAS globs every nested .gitignore, so app/mobile/.gitignore's
    `proto/**` stripped the stubs and Metro failed to resolve @/proto/bugs_pb.
    
    Add a repo-root .easignore. When present it replaces the whole .gitignore tree
    (eas-cli stops reading nested .gitignores), so it scopes the upload to
    app/mobile and mirrors app/mobile/.gitignore's rules — minus proto/**, which is
    deliberately kept so the artifact stubs reach EAS without being regenerated.
    .git and node_modules are dropped by EAS regardless.
    
    Scoping to app/mobile is safe for OTA continuity: fingerprint.config.js and
    .fingerprintignore reference only files inside app/mobile (no ../ sources), and
    the proto stubs are JS, not a fingerprint input — so the runtimeVersion is
    unchanged. Verified the rules with git check-ignore (proto stubs + OTA certs
    kept; native dirs, secrets, and the rest of the monorepo excluded; modules/*/ios
    sources preserved).
    
