    Add composite index on moderation_states (object_type, visibility)
    
    Queries filtering moderation_states by both object_type and visibility
    (e.g. counting shadowed group chats) were slow (~12ms) because the
    existing ix_moderation_states_id_visibility index is on (id, visibility).
    Postgres could filter on visibility via the index but had to scan every
    matching row to filter on object_type.
    
    The new ix_moderation_states_type_visibility index on (object_type,
    visibility) lets Postgres satisfy both conditions directly from the
    index, turning the query into a fast index-only scan.
    
