Author: Aapeli <git@aapelivuorinen.com>
Date:   Sun Mar 29 21:56:48 2026 -0400

    Use HTTP/2 between nginx and envoy to fix request queueing
    
    Nginx was proxying to envoy using HTTP/1.1 without keepalive, meaning
    each concurrent API request required a new TCP connection and requests
    were effectively serialized. This caused visible queueing in the browser
    when a page load issued multiple API calls simultaneously.
    
    Switch to HTTP/2 upstream (supported since nginx 1.25.1, we run 1.29)
    with a keepalive pool, allowing all concurrent requests to multiplex
    over a single connection to envoy.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

[33mcommit e69a712b285e8b689b764225d28e45ed4c9dc768[m
Author: Aapeli <git@aapelivuorinen.com>
Date:   Sun Mar 29 21:51:14 2026 -0400

    Optimize unseen host request count queries in Ping endpoint
    
    Rewrite the unseen sent/received host request count queries from
    JOIN + COUNT(DISTINCT) to EXISTS + COUNT(*). This allows Postgres to
    use a semi join that short-circuits after finding the first unseen
    message per host request, eliminating the need for a full join, sort,
    and deduplication.
    
    Before (sent, ~124ms): planner chose GiST index at 2.3ms/loop × 52,
    plus sort for DISTINCT.
    
    After (sent, 0.7ms): semi join short-circuits, users/moderation joins
    never executed when no unseen messages exist.
    
    After (received, 7.3ms): uses B-tree ix_users_active at 0.008ms/loop
    instead of GiST, semi join avoids full message scan.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

