    fix map click event handlers being called twice
    
    When an active feature on the map was clicked, both the
    `handleMapUserClick` and `handleMapClickAway` callbacks where called.
    
    Reason for this was the order in which these event callbacks are
    initiated. `handleMapUserClick` calls prevent default on the event object
    and `handleMapClickAway` checks if `event.preventDefault()` was called
    already. So handleMapUserClick should be bound before
    handleMapClickAway.
    
    Also removed an (imho) unneeded dependency of the useEffect hook.

